# The licensed vintage store at the repository root (never committed — see CLAUDE.md /
# STEP1 licensing discipline). ANCHORED with a leading slash: the unanchored `data/`
# this line used to read matched ANY directory named `data` at any depth, which silently
# excluded the entire `src/ah/data/` package (all of Step 1's data layer), every
# synthetic connector fixture under `tests/fixtures/data/`, and `docs/data/`. Those are
# source, tests and documentation, not licensed data, and they must be committed.
/data/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml

# Environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# uv
# (uv.lock IS committed; the venv is not)

# IDE / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*

# Step 2 experiments (local-first; manifests may be kept manually)
experiments/
.superpowers/

# Provenance-script outputs (scripts/compute_campaign_reference.py,
# measure_seal_evidence.py, measure_block_length_window.py, measure_mc_error_grid.py).
# Large, derived, and reproducible bit-for-bit from the sealed parameters against the
# sealed campaign vintage -- which is the point: `pre-registration.yaml` seals the
# parameters and quotes the numbers, so the JSON is a local check, not an artifact.
/reference-run*.json
/seal-evidence.json
# WP2.8b block-batching evidence (scripts/verify_block_batching.py): synthetic
# artifacts + reference ensembles, reproducible from the script and the pinned
# checkpoint, so the numbers are quoted in CHANGELOG/progress rather than stored.
/.verify-block-batching/
/block-length-window.json
/mc-error-grid.json

# WP2.4 battery evidence. The per-seed battery reports are large (~650 KB of JSON and
# ~110 KB of markdown each, three seeds) and reproduce bit-for-bit from
# `scripts/run_bootstrap_battery.py` against the sealed campaign vintage -- the same
# reasoning as the provenance-script outputs above. `artifacts/wp24/summary.json` IS
# committed and is the exception: it carries the verdict, every enforce gate, the
# per-comparison band-exceedance census and the conditional suite, it is what every later
# PR diffs `bootstrap-v1` against, and -- unlike the provenance outputs above -- no sealed
# document quotes those numbers, so nothing else in the repository would hold them.
/artifacts/*
!/artifacts/wp24/
/artifacts/wp24/*
!/artifacts/wp24/summary.json
# WP2.7 battery evidence, same reasoning: the per-seed reports (~700 KB JSON +
# markdown) reproduce bit-for-bit from scripts/run_joinery_battery.py against the
# sealed vintage and the pinned L1/L2 artifacts; the summary (verdict, enforce
# gates, support/reconciliation distributions) and the assembly report (the
# waypoint-tolerance record and the complete acceptance-filter rejection log --
# the WP2.7 evidence the sealed battery report has no line for) are what later
# PRs diff against, and no sealed document quotes those numbers.
!/artifacts/wp27/
/artifacts/wp27/*
!/artifacts/wp27/summary.json
!/artifacts/wp27/joinery-assembly-report.md
# WP-DATA-VOLEXT: the backcast provenance IS the auditable record (fit, HAC
# covariance, residual pool, full validation vs the AM-2026-08-09-001
# thresholds) and the D2 contract regenerates the ensemble from it -- nothing
# else in the repository would hold these numbers.
!/artifacts/volext/
/artifacts/volext/*
!/artifacts/volext/equity-vol-backcast-provenance.json
# WP2.8 (hier-diffusion-v1) evidence, same reasoning as WP2.4/WP2.7 above: the
# per-seed battery reports reproduce bit-for-bit from
# scripts/run_diffusion_battery.py against the sealed vintage, the pinned L1/L2
# artifacts and the pinned checkpoint. Four things ARE committed because nothing
# else in the repository would hold them: the summary (verdict, enforce gates,
# support/reconciliation distributions), the battery-and-diagnostics report (the
# reconciliation-shrinkage comparison against WP2.7's baseline), the COMPLETE
# TUNING LOG plus its selection record -- the sealed tuning_protocol's own
# forking-paths evidence, which tests/test_blocks_tuning.py machine-checks -- and
# the monthly-tier neighborhood table (WP2.8's stated acceptance evidence).
!/artifacts/wp28/
/artifacts/wp28/*
!/artifacts/wp28/summary.json
!/artifacts/wp28/wp28-battery-report.md
!/artifacts/wp28/tuning-log.jsonl
!/artifacts/wp28/selection.json
!/artifacts/wp28/neighborhood.md
!/artifacts/wp28/neighborhood.json
!/artifacts/wp28/ig-spread-diagnosis.md
!/artifacts/wp28/ig-spread-diagnosis.json
# WP2.7b (regime-conditional ig_spread band) evidence, same reasoning as WP2.4 /
# WP2.7 / WP2.8 above: the per-seed battery reports reproduce bit-for-bit from the
# battery scripts against the sealed vintage and the pinned artifacts, so only the
# things nothing else in the repository would hold are committed -- the two battery
# summaries (the verdicts that SUPERSEDE WP2.7's and WP2.8's under the new band),
# the estimator + old-vs-new re-measurement record, and its raw numbers.
!/artifacts/wp27b/
/artifacts/wp27b/*
!/artifacts/wp27b/spread-band.md
!/artifacts/wp27b/spread-band-remeasurement.json
!/artifacts/wp27b/battery-joinery/
/artifacts/wp27b/battery-joinery/*
!/artifacts/wp27b/battery-joinery/summary.json
!/artifacts/wp27b/battery-joinery/joinery-assembly-report.md
!/artifacts/wp27b/battery-diffusion/
/artifacts/wp27b/battery-diffusion/*
!/artifacts/wp27b/battery-diffusion/summary.json
!/artifacts/wp27b/battery-diffusion/wp28-battery-report.md
# WP2.9 (hier-flow-v1) evidence, same reasoning as WP2.4 / WP2.7 / WP2.8 above:
# the bake-off numbers reproduce bit-for-bit from scripts/run_sampler_bakeoff.py
# against the sealed vintage, the pinned L1/L2 artifacts and the two pinned
# checkpoints. What IS committed is what nothing else in the repository would
# hold: the COMPLETE TUNING LOG plus its selection record -- the sealed
# tuning_protocol's forking-paths evidence for the SECOND sampler, which
# tests/test_blocks_flow.py machine-checks -- the like-for-like bake-off table
# and its raw numbers, the companion measurements (search summary, guidance
# ablation, batching evidence, throughput), and the monthly-tier neighborhood
# table (the stated acceptance evidence).
!/artifacts/wp29/
/artifacts/wp29/*
!/artifacts/wp29/tuning-log.jsonl
!/artifacts/wp29/selection.json
!/artifacts/wp29/bakeoff.md
!/artifacts/wp29/bakeoff.json
!/artifacts/wp29/bakeoff-notes.md
!/artifacts/wp29/neighborhood.md
!/artifacts/wp29/neighborhood.json
# WP2.11 part 1 (severe test) evidence, same reasoning as WP2.4 / WP2.7 / WP2.8 /
# WP2.7b above: the per-cell battery reports reproduce from
# scripts/run_severe_test.py against the sealed vintage and the pinned artifacts,
# so only what nothing else in the repository holds is committed -- the generated
# report, its raw numbers, the six-cell grid summary, the cycle-forcing
# sensitivity measurement, and the severe checkpoint hashes.
!/artifacts/wp211/
/artifacts/wp211/*
!/artifacts/wp211/SEVERE-TEST.md
!/artifacts/wp211/severe-test.json
!/artifacts/wp211/severe-grid.json
!/artifacts/wp211/cycle-sensitivity.json
!/artifacts/wp211/severe-checkpoints.json
# WP2.11 part 2b: the same three products for the diffusion co-primary, on the
# same rule. The allowlist above is per-file, so a second family's report is
# ignored by default and silently -- `git commit` reported success while the
# report it described was never staged. Caught by reading the commit's own file
# count against what it claimed. Any third family needs three more lines here.
!/artifacts/wp211/SEVERE-TEST-DIFFUSION.md
!/artifacts/wp211/severe-test-diffusion.json
!/artifacts/wp211/severe-grid-diffusion.json

